Problem (Geometry, Level 4):
In the diagram below, $\triangle ABC$ is a right triangle with $\angle C = 90^\circ$. Point $D$ lies on side $AC$ such that $AD = 3$ and $DC = 6$. Point $E$ lies on side $BC$ such that $BE = 4$ and $EC = 8$. If the area of $\triangle CDE$ is 24 square units, what is the area of $\triangle ABC$?

[asy]
pair A,B,C,D,E;
C=(0,0);
A=(0,9);
B=(12,0);
D=(0,6);
E=(8,0);
draw(A--B--C--cycle);
draw(D--E);
label("$A$",A,NW);
label("$B$",B,SE);
label("$C$",C,SW);
label("$D$",D,W);
label("$E$",E,S);
label("3", (0,7.5), W);
label("6", (0,3), W);
label("4", (10,0), S);
